ttps://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-14T02:40:40Z","updated_at":"2026-07-14T02:40:40Z","body":"I feel like maybe that's not even the right solution because it probably still breaks for nested classes? As of 4.5 nested classes only highlight the toplevel script's members rather than the nested classes' members","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4964885218/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4966784719","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107941#issuecomment-4966784719","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107941","id":4966784719,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKAsezw","user":{"login":"zuranthus","id":7449346,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NDkzNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7449346?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zuranthus","html_url":"https://github.com/zuranthus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zuranthus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zuranthus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zuranthus/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zuranthus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zuranthus/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zuranthus/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zuranthus/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zuranthus/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zuranthus/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-14T08:09:43Z","updated_at":"2026-07-14T08:09:43Z","body":">I feel like maybe that's not even the right solution because it probably still breaks for nested classes? \n\n@sockeye-d I only tried to fix the original report - that the highlight doesn't update until the script is saved - without changing the highlighting itself.\nI think it can be fixed too, the parser seems to have the info on the nested classes and their members. I can verify that in a bit 🕐 ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4966784719/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4974116307","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107941#issuecomment-4974116307","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107941","id":4974116307,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKHr90w","user":{"login":"zuranthus","id":7449346,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NDkzNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7449346?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zuranthus","html_url":"https://github.com/zuranthus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zuranthus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zuranthus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zuranthus/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zuranthus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zuranthus/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zuranthus/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zuranthus/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zuranthus/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zuranthus/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-14T21:22:20Z","updated_at":"2026-07-14T21:22:20Z","body":"It is possible to highlight all nested classes' members:\n<img width=\"1326\" height=\"1256\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/98f1b22b-244e-428a-bb79-1d67277f05b9\" />\n\nThough since the highlighter is not context-aware, some identifiers can be highlighted incorrectly as a result. For example, if a nested member has the same name as a local variable, the local variable will be highlighted as a member:\n<img width=\"662\" height=\"272\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/da955b0a-28d3-4f83-9e8c-cacefbb57b64\" />\nI believe it is a preexisting issue that can't be fixed without overhauling the parser implementation (and therefore definitely out of scope of my small fix).\n\nHighlighting more identifiers as members may make it worse - increase the chance of highlighting something in a wrong way. But maybe it is worth it anyway 🤷🏻 \n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4974116307/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]